4:["$","article",null,{"className":"post-body","children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"post-sec","id":"what-meme-tokenomics-is","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"no","children":"01"}],"What meme coin tokenomics is"]}],["$","p",null,{"children":["For a community token, \"tokenomics\" is the design of three things: the ",["$","b",null,{"children":"supply"}]," (total amount and whether it can grow), the ",["$","b",null,{"children":"distribution"}]," (who holds it), and the ",["$","b",null,{"children":"controls"}]," (limits and ownership). These choices shape how the token can be used and shared — they don't create fame or demand on their own."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":["This guide is about strategy, not the mechanics of creation. If you want the creation steps, see the companion guide ",["$","a",null,{"href":"/create-meme-coin-bnb-chain","children":"how to create a meme coin on BNB Chain"}],". For the underlying BEP-20 principles, ",["$","a",null,{"href":"/bep20-tokenomics","children":"BEP-20 tokenomics"}]," is the general reference for supply and decimals."]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"post-sec","id":"big-number","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"no","children":"02"}],"Why a big supply number doesn't create value"]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"A common pattern is a very large supply with a very small display price. The huge number may look attractive, but supply size by itself has no market effect — it's a display choice recorded in the contract."}],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","i",null,{"className":"fa-solid fa-circle-check","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"A contract doesn't know or care what the coin \"should\" be worth; it only enforces your configured supply."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","i",null,{"className":"fa-solid fa-circle-check","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Doubling the supply does not double attention, adoption or price."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","i",null,{"className":"fa-solid fa-circle-check","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"What actually matters is whether the token is useful, shareable and distributed in a way a community can participate in."}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"callout","children":[["$","i",null,{"className":"fa-solid fa-circle-info","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Nothing here predicts or promotes value. A meme coin's design should fit what a community does with it — not chase a particular price."}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"post-sec","id":"supply-decimals","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"no","children":"03"}],"Choosing total supply and decimals"]}],["$","p",null,{"children":["Total supply is entered during configuration and can't be changed later (unless mintable — see ",["$","a",null,{"href":"#fixed-vs-mintable","children":"section 05"}],"). Decimals control display granularity: ",["$","b",null,{"children":"18"}]," is the BEP-20 default, ",["$","b",null,{"children":"0"}]," displays whole numbers."]}],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","i",null,{"className":"fa-solid fa-circle-check","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Pick a supply your intended distribution can meaningfully use. A round, memorable number is fine."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","i",null,{"className":"fa-solid fa-circle-check","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Remember base units: with 18 decimals, a supply of 1,000,000,000 means 1,000,000,000 × 10",["$","sup",null,{"children":"18"}]," base units on-chain."]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","i",null,{"className":"fa-solid fa-circle-check","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Decimals and total supply are fixed at deployment, just like the token name and symbol."}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":["The ",["$","a",null,{"href":"/features#supply-controls","children":"supply controls"}]," section of the features page shows exactly what the builder accepts in each field."]}]]}],"$L10","$L11","$L12","$L13","$L14","$L15","$L16","$L17","$L18"]}]
